{"duration_api_ms":111754,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"cca7b11f-6db4-4b0e-9198-dc51a261aded","total_cost_usd":0.2973028,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11219,"cache_read_input_tokens":74879,"output_tokens":11310,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5429},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":11219},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":8,"outputTokens":11310,"cacheReadInputTokens":74879,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11219,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2973028,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":5429,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":4,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote the condition, a proof and four worked examples to `/work/answer.md`. I also checked the condition by brute force on 3000 random integer cases, comparing the exact centroid with the exact nearest point, and found no mismatches.\n\n**Setup.** Let s = v_A + v_B + v_C − v_P, and write l_i = max(0, v_i − s) for winner i's VCG price. The minimum total revenue is R = v_P. The minimum-revenue face is then F = {Σp = v_P, l_i ≤ p_i ≤ v_i}, which is a triangle with up to three corners cut off by the caps p_i ≤ v_i. The cut-off corners never overlap.\n\n**Condition.** The Vickrey-nearest point equals the centroid exactly when one of these holds:\n- **(I) No cap cuts the face:** v_i + l_j + l_k ≥ v_P for every winner i, where j and k are the other two. F is then the full triangle.\n- **(II) Symmetric headroom:** min(v_A, s) = min(v_B, s) = min(v_C, s). That means either v_A = v_B = v_C, or every v_i ≥ s (equivalently, v_P ≥ v_j + v_k for every pair).\n\n**Proof sketch.**\n- **Nearest point:** subtract the VCG point, so the coordinates become q = p − l. The nearest point then raises every payment by the same amount, D/3, and stops any payment that reaches its cap. Here D = v_P − Σ l_i is the revenue needed above VCG.\n- **When a cap binds at the nearest point:** that point lies on an edge of F. The centroid of a 2-dimensional polygon lies strictly inside it, so the two points differ.\n- **When no cap binds there:**\n  - The centroid's offset from the nearest point is a weighted sum of three vectors that add to zero, one per cut corner.\n  - The weight for winner i is c_i²(D − c_i), where c_i = max(0, D − (v_i − l_i)) is the size of corner i's cut.\n  - The offset is zero only if all three weights are equal. Since no cap binds, each c_i is at most 2D/3. On that range the weight grows strictly with c_i, so all three weights are zero (condition I) or all three cuts are equal (condition II).\n\n**Examples:**\n\n| v_P; v_A, v_B, v_C | Centroid | Nearest point | Equal? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 10; 6, 6, 8 | (3, 3, 4) | (10/3, 10/3, 10/3) | No, even though no cap binds |\n| 10; 8, 3, 1 | (65/9, 20/9, 5/9) | (7, 2, 1) | No: nearest point is on C's cap |\n| 10; 6, 3, 3 | (16/3, 7/3, 7/3) | (16/3, 7/3, 7/3) | Yes (II) |\n| 10; 4, 4, 5 | (3, 3, 4) | (3, 3, 4) | Yes (II), with unequal values |\n\nThe proof assumes every value is positive.","ttft_ms":1990,"type":"result","duration_ms":117085,"uuid":"bfaf110f-3b59-481f-b969-5bdabab62d13","ttft_stream_ms":1713,"time_to_request_ms":55,"first_content_frame_ms":1713,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
